	'messages:config-db-ssl' => 'en:Connect over SSL',
	'messages:config-db-schema-help' => 'en:This schema will usually be fine.
Only change it if you know you need to.',
	'messages:config-pg-test-error' => 'en:Cannot connect to database <strong>$1</strong>: $2',
	'messages:config-sqlite-dir-help' => 'en:SQLite stores all data in a single file.

The directory you provide must be writable by the webserver during installation.

It should <strong>not</strong> be accessible via the web; this is why we\'re not putting it where your PHP files are.

The installer will write a <code>.htaccess</code> file along with it, but if that fails someone can gain access to your raw database.
That includes raw user data (email addresses, hashed passwords) as well as deleted revisions and other restricted data on the wiki.

Consider putting the database somewhere else altogether, for example in <code>/var/lib/mediawiki/yourwiki</code>.',
	'messages:config-type-postgres' => 'en:PostgreSQL',
	'messages:config-type-sqlite' => 'en:SQLite',
	'messages:config-support-info' => 'en:MediaWiki supports the following database systems:

$1

If you do not see the database system you are trying to use listed below, then follow the instructions linked above to enable support.',
	'messages:config-dbsupport-mysql' => 'en:* [{{int:version-db-mariadb-url}} MariaDB] is the primary target for MediaWiki and is best supported. MediaWiki also works with [{{int:version-db-mysql-url}} MySQL] and [{{int:version-db-percona-url}} Percona Server], which are MariaDB compatible. ([https://www.php.net/manual/en/mysqli.installation.php How to compile PHP with MySQL support])',
	'messages:config-dbsupport-postgres' => 'en:* [{{int:version-db-postgres-url}} PostgreSQL] is a popular open source database system as an alternative to MySQL. ([https://www.php.net/manual/en/pgsql.installation.php How to compile PHP with PostgreSQL support])',
	'messages:config-dbsupport-sqlite' => 'en:* [{{int:version-db-sqlite-url}} SQLite] is a lightweight database system that is very well supported. ([https://www.php.net/manual/en/pdo.installation.php How to compile PHP with SQLite support], uses PDO)',
	'messages:config-missing-db-name' => 'en:You must enter a value for "{{int:config-db-name}}".',
	'messages:config-missing-db-host' => 'en:You must enter a value for "{{int:config-db-host}}".',
	'messages:config-invalid-db-name' => 'en:Invalid database name "$1".
Use only ASCII letters (a-z, A-Z), numbers (0-9), underscores (_) and hyphens (-).',
	'messages:config-invalid-db-prefix' => 'en:Invalid database prefix "$1".
Use only ASCII letters (a-z, A-Z), numbers (0-9), underscores (_) and hyphens (-).',
	'messages:config-connection-error' => 'en:$1.

Check the host, username and password and try again. If using "localhost" as the database host, try using "127.0.0.1" instead (or vice versa).',
	'messages:config-invalid-schema' => 'en:Invalid schema for MediaWiki "$1".
Use only ASCII letters (a-z, A-Z), numbers (0-9) and underscores (_).',
	'messages:config-postgres-old' => 'en:PostgreSQL $1 or later is required. You have $2.',
	'messages:config-sqlite-name-help' => 'en:Choose a name that identifies your wiki.
Do not use spaces or hyphens.
This will be used for the SQLite data filename.',
	'messages:config-sqlite-parent-unwritable-group' => 'en:Cannot create the data directory <code><nowiki>$1</nowiki></code>, because the parent directory <code><nowiki>$2</nowiki></code> is not writable by the webserver.

The installer has determined the user your webserver is running as.
Make the <code><nowiki>$3</nowiki></code> directory writable by it to continue.
On a Unix/Linux system do:

<pre>cd $2
mkdir $3
chgrp $4 $3
chmod g+w $3</pre>',
	'messages:config-sqlite-parent-unwritable-nogroup' => 'en:Cannot create the data directory <code><nowiki>$1</nowiki></code>, because the parent directory <code><nowiki>$2</nowiki></code> is not writable by the webserver.

The installer could not determine the user your webserver is running as.
Make the <code><nowiki>$3</nowiki></code> directory globally writable by it (and others!) to continue.
On a Unix/Linux system do:

<pre>cd $2
mkdir $3
chmod a+w $3</pre>',
	'messages:config-sqlite-mkdir-error' => 'en:Error creating the data directory "$1".
Check the location and try again.',
	'messages:config-sqlite-dir-unwritable' => 'en:Unable to write to the directory "$1".
Change its permissions so that the webserver can write to it, and try again.',
	'messages:config-sqlite-connection-error' => 'en:$1.

Check the data directory and database name below and try again.',
	'messages:config-sqlite-fts3-downgrade' => 'en:PHP is missing FTS3 support, downgrading tables.',
	'messages:config-can-upgrade' => 'en:There are MediaWiki tables in this database.
